<Article
  title="Build your own, without a wallet"
  description="The Aura builder is a tool. Walk the clearing and set a shell on this site, or build it from the GitHub source."
  kicker="Builder"
  date="2026-09-30"
>
  <p>The entrance is the clearing: a film, then a walk from the ridge to the cabin, up onto the deck, and out to the tub. That journey was built for aurahomes.fun. It now lives on this site as the <a href="/builder">builder</a>, in the same brand as the room.</p>
  <h2>What was taken out</h2>
  <p>The earlier telling of that walk ran through a wallet, escrow on a chain, a hackathon, and a token. None of that is in this tab. There is no connect button, no testnet, and no dashboard of funds. The night control and the sound of the clearing stayed, because they belong to the place, not to the chain.</p>
  <h2>What you actually do</h2>
  <p>You scroll the clearing. At the end you set three things: the use, the glass, and the length. The page writes one sentence, and it stays in the browser. Nothing on that page is for sale. If you want to build the shell yourself, the source is on <a href="https://github.com/kr8tiv-ai/aura-homes">GitHub</a>.</p>
  <h2>What the picture is, and is not</h2>
  <p>The clearing shows the cabin, the deck, and the tub. It does not yet show lettuce on the wall or a condenser on the roof. Those are on the <a href="/farms">farm</a> and <a href="/water">water</a> pages. The builder is the walk, and the brief. The photographs of the other uses are the other uses.</p>
  <p>If you want the whole argument in one place, start with <a href="/journal/one-shell">one shell</a>.</p>
</Article>
